slide('Useful data. Bounded authority.','AegisPay / Stellar Testnet','PREPARED · 09 NOV 2026','''
<div class="hero"><div><div class="wordmark"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-label="AegisPay mark"><path d="M4 40 25 5h8L12 40Zm17-10 6-10 17 20H31Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>AegisPay<span>.</span></div>
<h1 id="s1">Useful data.<br><em>Bounded authority.</em></h1>
<p class="lead">Let a release assistant choose a specialist report.<br>Keep spending permission outside its prompt.</p></div>
<div class="hero-seal"><span class="orbit-label">THE ACHIEVED BOUNDARY</span><strong>01</strong><span>verified Noir / Velo<br>authorization</span><small>Historical Testnet proof · 7 Nov</small></div></div>
<div class="bottomline"><span>Salvador Vincent Javier · solo builder</span><span>Public proof viewer live · full purchasing agent unfinished</span></div>''',
'Imagine a release assistant that needs one specialist report to write a useful dependency triage note. The model should choose the information; its owner should control the spending authority. AegisPay explores that boundary on Stellar Testnet. We have proved one Noir authorization through Velo, with an inspectable public proof viewer.',25,a(site,'Public proof viewer')+' · '+a(repo,'Source'),True)
slide('Should we ship this dependency update?','01 / Start with a useful task','HYPOTHETICAL CUSTOMER','''
<h2 id="s2">Should we ship this<br>dependency update?</h2>
<div class="task-split"><div class="task-quote"><span class="label">A small developer team asks</span><p>“Review <strong>demo-parser</strong>.<br>Buy only what helps a<br>basic release triage note.”</p><div class="budget-pill">Total task ceiling · 0.10 Testnet XLM</div></div>
<div class="task-detail"><div class="label">Why paid data could matter</div><h3>Metadata names the report.<br>It cannot answer the task.</h3><p>A specialist report could add advisory context and known limitations beyond the free listing.</p><div class="thin-rule"></div><p>The useful output: a sourced triage note that says what remains unknown.</p></div></div>
<p class="caption">Illustrative scenario only. demo-parser and both reports are fictional; no security assessment or delivered answer is claimed.</p>''',
'Our proposed user is a small team building a release assistant. The task: review the fictional demo-parser dependency and write a basic triage note, within point one Testnet XLM. Free metadata describes a report, but specialist content could add the advisory context the assistant lacks. That is the reason to buy. The useful output would cite its source and say what remains unknown. This is an illustrative task with fictional reports.',35,a(base+'docs/prd.md','Intended resource workflow')+' · Fictional reports; unvalidated customer hypothesis.')
slide('Choose the information. Keep the rules.','02 / The intended decision','NOT AN EXECUTED PURCHASE','''
<h2 id="s3">Choose the information.<br><em>Keep the rules.</em></h2>
<div class="offer-head"><span>Fictional specialist reports</span><span>Illustrative Testnet price</span><span>Per-payment cap: 0.10 XLM</span></div>
<div class="offer"><div><h3>QuickSignal</h3><p>Basic advisory context</p></div><div class="price">0.03 <small>XLM</small></div><div class="decision">Within the example cap</div></div>
<div class="offer"><div><h3>DeepTrace</h3><p>Extended investigation</p></div><div class="price">0.12 <small>XLM</small></div><div class="decision stop">Above the example cap</div></div>
<div class="choice-line"><div><b>Agent decides usefulness</b><p>Buy relevant data, or buy nothing.</p></div><span class="divider">/</span><div><b>Trusted tools control permission</b><p>Current quote, task budget and signing.</p></div></div>
<p class="caption">No completed model choice or report delivery. Contract cap + expiry + finite escrow are distinct from the application task budget.</p>''',
'QuickSignal is the basic fixture at three hundred thousand stroops. DeepTrace is the extended fixture at one point two million, above the one-million cap. Affordability alone is not an intelligent choice: the agent should inspect current offers and buy nothing when data adds no value. Trusted tools own the quote, task budget and signing. Noir separately enforces per-payment policy, expiry and finite escrow. This intended workflow has not completed a model purchase or report delivery.',45,a(base+'docs/evidence/finals-pitch-refresh/task-016.md#current-sources','Scenario / source provenance')+' · 300000 / 1200000 stroops; 1000000-stroop example cap.')
slide('Two SDKs. The same authorization.','03 / Actual integration proof','HISTORICAL · 07 NOV','''
<h2 id="s4">Two SDKs.<br><em>The same authorization.</em></h2>
<div class="integration"><div><span class="stepno">01</span><h3>Noir</h3><p>Policy and escrow<br>prepare authorization.</p><small>Agent key signs server-side</small></div><span class="flow-arrow">→</span><div><span class="stepno">02</span><h3>Velo Gas</h3><p>Sponsor and submit<br>that signed invocation.</p><small>Persist identity before handoff</small></div><span class="flow-arrow">→</span><div><span class="stepno">03</span><h3>Independent proof</h3><p>Match the successful<br>envelope, call and event.</p><small>Reconcile inner / outer identity</small></div></div>
<div class="proof-strip"><strong>Our contribution</strong><span>Exact integration + evidence mapping.<br>A dependable resource-specific workflow is the next gate.</span></div>
<p class="caption">Noir supplies policy / escrow; Velo supplies sponsorship / submission. Caps, agent wallets and HTTP 402 alone are not unique.</p>''',
'Here is the achieved integration. Noir prepares the escrow authorization. The agent key signs server-side. Velo Gas sponsors and submits that same signed invocation, with its identity persisted before handoff. Independent RPC evidence matches the successful envelope, exact invocation and Noir event to Velo execution. Event alone is insufficient: it omits asset and agent. Noir owns the policy and escrow primitives; Velo supplies sponsorship and submission. Our contribution is this exact integration and evidence mapping, toward a dependable resource workflow. Generic wallets, caps and payment challenges already exist.',45,a(hist,'Saved independent evidence')+' · '+a(base+'src/server/integrations/stellar-evidence.ts','Verifier'),True)
slide('One payment. A readable receipt.','04 / Inspect the result','SAVED TESTNET RUN · 07 NOV',f'''
<div class="receipt-grid"><div><h2 id="s5">One payment.<br>A readable receipt.</h2><div class="receipt-amount">0.03<span>Testnet XLM</span></div><p>300000 stroops authorized<br>into merchant-pending escrow.</p><p class="muted" style="margin-top:24px">A separate merchant claim<br>later cleared pending to zero.</p></div>
<div class="receipt"><div class="receipt-top"><b>AEGISPAY / HISTORICAL PROOF</b><span>MATCHED</span></div><div class="receipt-row"><span>Authorization</span><strong>One verified operation</strong></div><div class="receipt-row"><span>Escrow</span><strong>1.00 → 0.97 XLM</strong></div><div class="receipt-row"><span>Merchant pending</span><strong>0 → 0.03 → 0 XLM</strong></div><div class="receipt-row"><span>Independent match</span><strong>Envelope + call + event</strong></div><div class="receipt-links">{a('https://stellar.expert/explorer/testnet/tx/'+hashes[0],'Inner authorization')}<br>{a('https://stellar.expert/explorer/testnet/tx/'+hashes[1],'Outer / event: same payment')}<br>{a('https://stellar.expert/explorer/testnet/tx/'+hashes[2],'Separate merchant claim')}</div></div></div>
<div class="refusal-line"><span class="stop-mark">×</span><p><strong>0.12 requested / 0.10 cap:</strong> actual contract simulation refused it.<br><span class="muted">Unsigned and unsubmitted; no included failed transaction.</span></p></div>''',
'This receipt describes one historical payment. The inner Noir authorization and fee-bump outer transaction map to the same operation; its event uses the outer hash. Three hundred thousand stroops moved into merchant-pending escrow. A separate merchant claim later cleared pending to zero. The labels link to the exact transactions. We also observed actual contract simulation refusing one point two million against the one-million cap: unsigned and unsubmitted. This proof establishes the payment integration; it does not establish a QuickSignal purchase.',40,a(hist,'Full historical proof / balances')+' · '+a(site,'Inspect the deployed viewer')+' · Historical policy expired 7 Nov, 15:32 UTC.')
slide('Unknown means hold.','05 / The boundary under uncertainty','OBSERVED APP ATTEMPT · 09 NOV',f'''
<h2 id="s6">Unknown means <em>hold.</em></h2><p class="lead sub">One persisted financial handoff. No verified outcome.</p>
<div class="unknown-metrics"><div><strong>300000</strong><span>stroops held</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>stroops spent in app ledger</span></div><div><strong>0</strong><span>report entitlements</span></div></div>
<div class="hold-path"><span>Saved purchase identity</span><b>→</b><strong>UNKNOWN</strong><b>→</b><span>Observe that identity</span></div>
<p class="hold-statement">No replacement payment. No report release.</p>
<p class="caption">Latest saved Velo status read: HTTP 409; prior RPC: NOT_FOUND. This is observed conservative behavior, not completed recovery.</p>''',
'The newer application attempt remains unknown after one persisted financial handoff. Its ledger holds three hundred thousand stroops, records zero spent and grants no report entitlement. The last saved Velo status read returned HTTP four-oh-nine; the prior RPC lookup was not found. Neither establishes success or definitive failure. The purchase keeps its original identity for observation, without a replacement payment or report release. This is conservative unresolved behavior, not completed recovery. One application handoff is our boundary, not a universal exactly-once execution guarantee.',40,a(base+'docs/evidence/finals-pitch-refresh/task-016.md#application-attempt','Persisted attempt')+' · '+a(base+'docs/evidence/finals-pitch-refresh/task-016.md#application-attempt','Saved status observation'),True)
slide('Start with one developer. And one data provider.','06 / The customer and revenue hypothesis','UNVALIDATED · NO EXISTING PARTNERS','''
<h2 id="s7">Start with one developer.<br>And one data provider.</h2>
<div class="pilot-equation"><div><span class="label">One developer</span><h3>A release assistant<br>with a real data gap</h3></div><b>+</b><div><span class="label">One specialist provider</span><h3>A useful report endpoint<br>with permission to integrate</h3></div></div>
<div class="pilot-measures"><div><span>01 / Usefulness</span><p>Does the report improve<br>a task they repeat?</p></div><div><span>02 / Reliability</span><p>Correct access, unresolved<br>duration, integration effort.</p></div><div><span>03 / Economics</span><p>Would a provider pay<br>for the gateway?</p></div></div>
<p class="caption">Revenue hypothesis: provider gateway subscription or fulfilled-request fee. Demand, willingness to pay, costs and margins are unvalidated.</p>''',
'The proposed pilot pairs one release-assistant developer with one specialist report provider. We want a real endpoint commitment and repeated use on an actual task. Measure whether the report improves the answer, then setup effort, correct access and unresolved duration. A provider subscription or fulfilled-request fee is an unvalidated revenue hypothesis. Model, hosting, RPC, sponsorship and support costs need measurement. We are seeking design partners; no customers, revenue or validated margins are claimed.',35,a(base+'docs/evidence/finals-pitch-refresh/task-016.md#business-hypotheses','Pilot / economics rationale')+' · Proposed design partners; no market-size or traction claim.')
slide('Next: one complete purchase. Verified end to end.','07 / The next measurable milestone','AEGISPAY · SAME SUBMITTED LINKS',f'''
<h2 id="s8">Next: one complete purchase.<br><em>Verified end to end.</em></h2>
<div class="closing-grid"><div><p class="ask">One agent developer.<br>One specialist report provider.<br>Technical feedback on the boundary.</p><p class="closing-next">Next gate: genuine model choice → verified report<br>→ sourced answer → demonstrated recovery.</p></div><div class="status-list"><div><span class="status-dot"></span><p><b>Proved</b><br>Historical Noir / Velo authorization + separate claim</p></div><div><span class="status-dot"></span><p><b>Live</b><br>Public recorded-proof viewer</p></div><div><span class="status-dot local"></span><p><b>Implemented locally</b><br>Workspaces, PostgreSQL, auth / wallet APIs, Gemini adapter</p></div><div><span class="status-dot open"></span><p><b>Open</b><br>Full model purchase, recovery and hosted release</p></div></div></div>
<div class="closing-links">{a(site,'aegispay-live.vercel.app')}{a(repo,'Source')}{a(pdf,'Submitted pitch PDF')}{a(folder,'Video folder')}</div>
<p class="caption">Video link is the recovered folder; new MP4 upload / playback is unverified. Five-minute pitch + three-minute Q&amp;A working format.</p>''',
'The next milestone is one complete useful purchase: genuine model choice, verified report access, a sourced answer and demonstrated recovery. Our public proof viewer is live. Workspaces, PostgreSQL foundations, private auth and wallet APIs, and a Gemini adapter exist locally; the complete purchasing and hosted release gates remain open. The submitted website, source, PDF and video folder stay at their existing links. We ask for one developer, one specialist provider and technical feedback to test that next milestone. Thank you.',35,a(base+'docs/evidence/finals-pitch-refresh/task-016.md#deployment','Deployment evidence')+' · '+a(base+'docs/evidence/finals-pitch-refresh/task-016.md#current-sources','Local backend evidence'),True)

